You regain `10d8 + 30` Hit Points and end any combination of three of the following affecting you:
- Blinded;
- Charmed;
- Deafened;
- Frightened;
- Paralyzed;
- Poisoned;
- Stunned;
- one disease;
- one poison;
- one level of Exhaustion.
A creature can benefit from this pill only once per Long Rest.

A creature eating the full banquet gains all the following benefits until its next Long Rest:
- +1 to saving throws;
- Temporary Hit Points equal to five times its Proficiency Bonus;
- Resistance to one damage type chosen from acid, cold, fire, lightning, poison, radiant, or necrotic;
- Advantage on one skill chosen when the banquet is served.
A creature can benefit from only one Sovereign Dao Banquet at a time.

wondrous.text:
After tapping a metal object for 1 minute, you learn:
- its primary metal or alloy;
- whether it is cracked, warped, improperly tempered, or structurally sound;
- whether it is Mortal or a supernatural treasure;
- its approximate treasure grade, if any.
You have Advantage on the next check made within 1 hour to repair or appraise that object. The hammer does not reveal hidden enchantment functions.

The cauldron can perform a 24-hour refinement ritual for one willing Beast or bonded companion. The ritual consumes appropriate harvested materials worth at least 5 Mid-Grade Spirit Stones.
At the ritual's end, choose one adaptation lasting until the creature completes its next Long Rest:
- gain Resistance to acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison;
- increase one movement Speed by 20 feet;
- gain a Climb or Swim Speed equal to its Speed;
- gain Temporary Hit Points equal to five times your Proficiency Bonus;
- treat its natural attacks as magical and add `1d6` damage of an appropriate elemental type.
A creature can receive one adaptation at a time. Permanent evolution requires its own progression rule, ingredients, and story procedure.

As a 10-minute procedure, plant the banner to create a 60-foot-radius camp formation for up to 8 hours.
While inside the formation:
- allied creatures cannot be surprised while conscious;
- ordinary weather does not extinguish fires or damage shelters;
- the attuned bearer knows when a Tiny or larger creature crosses the boundary;
- allies have Advantage on saving throws against magical sleep and dream intrusion.
The formation ends if the banner is moved, knocked down, or reduced to 0 Hit Points. The banner has AC 17 and 40 Hit Points.

The compass can survey a region during a 1-hour ritual performed on natural ground.
Choose a radius up to 100 miles. The compass reveals:
- major spirit-stone and mineral veins;
- Sovereign-grade or stronger geomantic disturbances;
- large sealed domains, artificial caverns, and buried complexes;
- the direction of the strongest natural Source concentration;
- whether the region's qi flow is stable, exhausted, corrupted, diverted, or concealed.
The compass provides a layered map but not exact treasure contents, passwords, creatures, or safe routes. An Imperial concealment can block a portion of the reading without creating false information.
The compass can perform one grand survey per Long Rest.

When a willing creature dies within 120 feet, you can use your Reaction to invite its soul into the lamp.
The soul can remain for up to **one year**. While sheltered:
- it can speak through the flame;
- it remembers its identity and life;
- it cannot be transformed into an Undead or consumed by a Sovereign-grade or weaker effect;
- effects restoring it to life treat the soul as present and willing;
- once per month, it can enter the dream of one willing creature sleeping within 1 mile and converse for up to 1 hour.
The soul can depart at any time. The lamp cannot capture an unwilling soul, force reincarnation, or determine the soul's next life.

The cauldron supports crafting and refinement up to Sovereign grade.
At the start of a project, assign each of its five chambers to Fire, Water, Earth, Metal, or Wood. The cauldron can simultaneously purify, temper, preserve, combine, and circulate compatible materials.
You gain a +3 bonus to relevant Alchemy, Blacksmith, Medicine, or material-refinement checks.
Once per Long Rest, choose one benefit for a project:
- reduce required crafting time by 25 percent;
- preserve all rare materials after a failed check;
- substitute one compatible material of the same grade for a missing phase component;
- produce 25 percent additional consumable yield.
The cauldron cannot bypass formulas, access requirements, or an Immortal ingredient.

The tablet can hold the willingly recorded names and memories of up to nine deceased ancestors or lineage teachers.
Once per Long Rest, perform a 10-minute rite to manifest their spectral court for 1 hour. The court can answer up to nine questions using its members' knowledge and perspectives.
During the manifestation, choose one blessing:
- **War:** allies within 30 feet gain +2 to initiative;
- **Wisdom:** allies have Advantage on Intelligence and Wisdom ability checks;
- **Guardianship:** allies gain Temporary Hit Points equal to three times your Proficiency Bonus;
- **Discipline:** allies have Advantage on saving throws against Charmed and Frightened.
A blessing lasts 1 hour. The court cannot reveal information its members never knew.

As a 10-minute ritual, place the pagoda on a stable surface to create a 300-foot-radius boundary for up to 8 hours.
Within the boundary:
- creatures cannot teleport or travel between planes against their will;
- hostile teleportation into or out of the area requires a Charisma saving throw against your item save DC;
- on a failed save, the teleportation is wasted and the creature takes `6d8` force damage;
- portals and extradimensional entrances of Sovereign grade or lower remain closed unless authorized during setup.
The boundary ends if the pagoda is moved or destroyed. It has AC 20 and 200 Hit Points.

The bell requires 8 hours to install and protects a 1-mile-radius area.
During setup, designate authorized creatures, tokens, roads, and entry conditions. The bell sounds when:
- a hostile force of ten or more creatures enters the area;
- a Sovereign-grade or stronger supernatural effect is activated;
- a creature crosses a designated boundary without authorization;
- a linked Formation Anchor is destroyed.
The bell identifies the triggering category and direction to authorized listeners.
Once per Long Rest, an authorized creature adjacent to the bell can use an Action to release a defensive peal. Hostile creatures of its choice within 300 feet make a Constitution saving throw against DC 19. On a failed save, a creature takes `10d8` thunder damage and is Stunned until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half damage and is not Stunned.

The pearl has 7 charges and regains `1d6 + 1` expended charges when you complete a Long Rest.
**Still the Waters.** As an Action, expend 3 charges and choose a point on a body of water within 300 feet. For up to 10 minutes, requiring Concentration, natural waves, currents, whirlpools, and undertows are suppressed in a 1-mile-radius area centered on that point.
Within the affected area:
- ordinary water becomes calm;
- vessels have Advantage on checks made to remain upright or navigate;
- creatures cannot be moved by natural currents;
- a hostile magical water effect of Sovereign grade or lower is suppressed if its creator fails an ability check against your item save DC.
The pearl cannot drain a sea, create land, or suppress an Imperial or Immortal ocean effect.

The spade can redirect a natural spirit vein during a 30-day project.
The project requires:
- a source and destination within 10 miles;
- a viable geomantic route;
- materials worth 20 High-Grade Spirit Stones;
- daily work by a creature proficient with an appropriate crafting or formation tool.
At completion, make an Intelligence check using the relevant tool against DC 20. On a success, the vein's primary flow is redirected to the destination without changing its total output. On a failure, the vein remains in place, half the materials are lost, and the region suffers unstable qi for 30 days.
The spade cannot create a vein, move an Imperial or world-root vein, or steal a vein through a stronger active formation.

The urn grows a sapling that creates a 300-foot-radius fertile sanctuary while planted in natural soil.
Within the sanctuary:
- ordinary plants grow at eight times their normal rate;
- Spiritual and Saint-grade plants grow at four times their normal rate;
- Sovereign-grade plants can survive when supplied with appropriate conditions;
- creatures completing a Long Rest gain Temporary Hit Points equal to twice their Proficiency Bonus;
- ordinary blight, drought, frost, and vermin do not harm cultivated plants.
The sapling can be uprooted during an 8-hour ritual and returns to urn form. If destroyed, it becomes dormant for one year unless restored by an Imperial life effect.

The crucible refines up to 1,000 pounds of ore during a 24-hour process.
Choose one operation:
- remove mundane impurities;
- separate mixed metals;
- condense trace spiritual metal;
- stabilize meteorite or star-metal;
- reduce raw ore to one-quarter its weight without losing useful material.
You gain a +3 bonus to Blacksmith or material-refinement checks made with the crucible.
Once per Long Rest, the crucible can convert materials worth 10 High-Grade Spirit Stones into one compatible Sovereign-grade metal component worth the same amount, provided at least one genuine sample of that metal is included.
It cannot create Imperial or Immortal material.

The casket can hold one willing creature, corpse, disembodied soul, or Nascent Soul-equivalent entity.
While sealed:
- the occupant does not age, breathe, eat, drink, or decay;
- poisons, diseases, curses, and ongoing conditions are suspended;
- the occupant is Unconscious but can choose to communicate telepathically with the attuned bearer within 30 feet;
- Sovereign-grade or weaker effects cannot locate, possess, consume, or transform the occupant.
Time passes normally outside, and the occupant gains no rest or recovery.
The casket can remain sealed indefinitely. Opening it requires an Action by the bearer or a DC 21 Intelligence (Arcana) check during a 1-hour ritual.

The bell requires 30 days to install and protects a 10-mile-radius sect domain.
It detects hostile armies, Imperial-grade power activations, planar breaches, major Formation damage, and registered members reduced to 0 Hit Points within the domain.
The bell can maintain three continuous domain blessings chosen during installation:
- Advantage on saving throws against Charmed and Frightened;
- resistance to ordinary extreme weather;
- authorized creatures cannot be surprised while conscious;
- hostile teleportation requires a DC 19 Charisma saving throw;
- linked Formation Anchors gain 100 Temporary Hit Points at dawn.
Once per month, the bell can release a Heaven Peal. Hostile creatures chosen by the bell's authorized keeper within 1 mile make a DC 19 Constitution saving throw, taking `20d8` thunder damage and becoming Stunned for 1 minute on a failure, repeating the save at the end of each turn. On success, they take half damage.

The furnace can craft, repair, combine, or purify treasures up to Imperial grade.
It maintains five independent phase chambers—Fire, Water, Earth, Metal, and Wood—and can process five linked projects simultaneously.
You gain a +4 bonus to relevant crafting checks.
Once per month, choose one Imperial refinement privilege:
- reduce one project's time by 50 percent;
- preserve all materials after a failed check;
- remove one Sovereign-grade curse or corruption automatically;
- merge two compatible Sovereign Treasures into one Imperial Treasure using a legal formula;
- raise one Sovereign material's normal ceiling to Imperial for that project.
It cannot craft an Immortal Artifact without an Immortal formula, material, facility, and story condition.

The seal requires 30 days to integrate with a mountain, city wall, sect valley, or fortress boundary no larger than 20 miles across.
While active:
- hostile teleportation and planar travel across the boundary fail unless the creature succeeds on a DC 19 Charisma saving throw;
- unauthorized underground movement is slowed to one-quarter normal speed;
- tunneling and earth-shaping effects of Sovereign grade or lower fail;
- the keeper knows when a Gargantuan creature, army, or Imperial effect crosses the boundary;
- linked gates can open or close as an Action by authorized seals.
The seal consumes the output of one major spirit vein or 1 Perfect Spirit Stone per month.

The pavilion contains ten thousand adaptive habitats within a stable extradimensional domain.
It can house up to:
- 1,000 willing Tiny or Small creatures;
- 500 Medium creatures;
- 200 Large creatures;
- 50 Huge creatures;
- 10 Gargantuan creatures.
Occupants receive breathable air, water, ordinary food, climate, shelter, and space appropriate to their nature. They can complete rests normally.
The pavilion records each occupant's observed traits, diet, behavior, injuries, lineage, and known abilities.
It cannot imprison an unwilling creature, manufacture rare ingredients, force reproduction, grant permanent evolution, or contain an Immortal creature without its consent.

The court can preserve the willing memory-presences of up to one hundred deceased ancestors, teachers, rulers, or lineage guardians.
Once per Long Rest, manifest the court in a 120-foot-radius area for 1 hour. The court can answer questions from its collective knowledge and grants all authorized allies in the area:
- Advantage on Intelligence and Wisdom saving throws;
- +2 to attack rolls and saving throws;
- immunity to being Frightened;
- Temporary Hit Points equal to five times their Proficiency Bonus when the court appears.
Once during the manifestation, the bearer can request **Ancestral Intercession**, causing every authorized ally in the area to regain `8d8` Hit Points.
The court cannot reveal knowledge none of its members possessed or bind an unwilling soul.

The tower surveys a 1,000-mile-radius region on the same plane.
Authorized observers can use its central mirror to view a known outdoor location within range for up to 1 hour, requiring Concentration. The view includes sight, sound, weather, and visible supernatural effects.
The tower continuously detects:
- Imperial power activations;
- planar breaches;
- armies larger than 1,000 creatures;
- major storms, earthquakes, eruptions, and celestial events;
- destruction of linked Formation Anchors.
Imperial concealment can contest observation with an ability check against DC 19. Immortal concealment blocks it automatically unless the effect says otherwise.

The scale has 9 charges and regains `1d8 + 1` after a Long Rest.
During a 10-minute hearing, place a willing creature's token, name, or blood on the scale and state one specific act, debt, oath, or harm.
The scale reveals:
- whether the creature sincerely accepts responsibility;
- whether the represented obligation remains materially unresolved;
- the broad magnitude of the unresolved consequence;
- whether another named party knowingly falsified the claim.
An unwilling creature can resist with a Charisma saving throw against your item save DC.
**Judgment.** Expend 5 charges to impose a 30-day karmic mark on a creature that failed the save. Whenever it knowingly repeats the judged act, it takes `10d10` psychic damage and the mark becomes visible. The scale cannot define morality, punish ambiguous conduct, or override an Immortal mandate.

The spade can relocate one major tree, sacred grove, spirit spring, mineral garden, or regional plant ecosystem during a 30-day project.
The source and destination must be on the same plane and within 1,000 miles. The project requires:
- a viable destination;
- materials worth 20 Perfect Spirit Stones;
- daily work by at least ten trained assistants;
- an Intelligence check using appropriate tools against DC 22.
On a success, the transplanted site retains its health, ordinary inhabitants, spiritual output, and local properties. On a failure, no relocation occurs, half the materials are lost, and both sites require 30 days to stabilize.
The spade cannot move a world tree, continental vein, city, or unwilling intelligent ecosystem.

The board can link to up to one hundred Formation Anchors within 100 miles.
The attuned bearer knows each linked anchor's location, condition, power reserve, active mode, and current breach status.
As an Action, the bearer can activate, deactivate, redirect, or change one authorized linked formation mode from any distance within the network.
The board has 9 Command charges and regains `1d8 + 1` after a Long Rest. Expend:
- **1 charge:** transfer up to 5 charges or equivalent power between linked anchors;
- **2 charges:** grant one linked anchor 200 Temporary Hit Points;
- **3 charges:** cause one formation effect to originate from a different linked anchor for 1 round;
- **5 charges:** maintain one linked formation for 1 minute without its normal Concentration requirement.
The board cannot seize an unauthorized formation or override an Immortal core.

The coffin can hold one willing creature, corpse, soul, Nascent Soul, or comparable spiritual body.
While sealed:
- time does not pass for the occupant;
- aging, decay, conditions, curses, poison, disease, and resource loss are suspended;
- the occupant cannot be located, possessed, transformed, consumed, or contacted by an Imperial-grade or weaker effect;
- the body and soul remain mutually anchored;
- resurrection or restoration effects treat all preserved components as present.
The occupant gains no rest, healing, training, or subjective experience.
Opening the coffin requires the attuned bearer, the occupant's consent if conscious, or a successful DC 25 Intelligence (Arcana) check during an 8-hour ritual.

The cabinet stores up to one thousand medicine doses, pills, ingredients, samples, and healer's tools without spoilage.
It has 20 Medicine charges and regains `2d8 + 4` when restocked during a Long Rest with supplies worth 1 Perfect Spirit Stone.
As an Action, expend:
- **1 charge:** restore `5d8 + 10` Hit Points;
- **2 charges:** end one poison or disease of Imperial grade or lower;
- **3 charges:** end one Charmed, Frightened, Paralyzed, or Stunned condition;
- **5 charges:** remove one level of Exhaustion;
- **10 charges:** restore one creature dead for no more than 1 minute to life with 1 Hit Point, provided its soul is willing and present.
A creature can lose only one level of Exhaustion to the cabinet per Long Rest. It cannot restore a destroyed soul or reverse an Immortal affliction.
